    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The full test surface is the single `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are an abstract base and a helper), and it's green \u2014 it exercises the exact new behavior: two owners joining an existing owner's household via `sharesHousehold: true` get back a matching, non-blank `householdId`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the shared-household feature in the Spring Boot PetClinic REST app. The scaffolding for `sharesHousehold` (the DTO field, duplicate-rejection logic, and `DuplicateHouseholdException`) already existed; what was missing was the `householdId` assignment and response field.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `householdId` property to the `Owner` response schema (the generator produces `OwnerDto.householdId`). `sharesHousehold` was already defined on `OwnerFields`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the persisted `householdId` field (`@Column(name = \"household_id\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the `household_id` column. This is required because tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema is driven entirely by these files.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Compute and assign the household id on create via a new `householdId(lastName, address)` helper. It's a **deterministic** function of the normalized last name + address (same trim/collapse-whitespace/lowercase rule already used by `rejectDuplicateHousehold`), formatted `HH-<12 hex of SHA-256>`. Because it's deterministic, every owner in the same household \u2014 including one that joins via `sharesHousehold: true` \u2014 gets the identical stable identifier, with no need to mutate existing records.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"householdId\", ignore = true)` on the `OwnerFieldsDto \u2192 Owner` mapping (a response-only field, mirroring `customerCode`); the `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` direction maps automatically.\n\nThe existing behavior is preserved: when `sharesHousehold` is false/omitted, a same-lastName-and-address create is still rejected with 409; when true, the create is allowed and the shared `householdId` is returned.",
